<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The first forward-looking feeling in the set.

    Everything else here is about something that already happened. This is about something that
    has not. The stage comes from one ratio: what is coming against what this colony has to meet
    it with. Both halves are things a colonist could actually notice - how rich the place looks,
    how long it has been quiet, whether they personally are holding a weapon, whether there is
    anything between them and the treeline.

    Psychopath is deliberately NOT nullified anywhere in this mod. Fear for your own skin is not
    an empathy, and a psychopath has as much interest in not being shot as anybody else. This is
    the one thing in the whole set they feel exactly like everyone else.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>DR_Dread</defName>
    <workerClass>Dread.ThoughtWorker_Dread</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <developmentalStageFilter>Adult</developmentalStageFilter>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>something is coming</label>
        <description>Nothing has happened. Nothing is wrong. I keep checking the treeline anyway.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-3</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>we are not ready for it</label>
        <description>I have counted what we have and counted what is out there, and I do not like the answer I keep getting.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-8</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>we cannot hold this place</label>
        <description>When it comes, and it is coming, we are not going to stop it. Everybody here knows that. Nobody says it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-14</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    The quiet. Separate from readiness on purpose, because it is a different feeling: this one
    gets worse precisely when nothing is happening, which no mood in this game has ever done.

    It is also true. RimWorld's storyteller really is winding up while nothing is happening, and
    a colonist who has been here a while really has learned that.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>DR_TooQuiet</defName>
    <workerClass>Dread.ThoughtWorker_TooQuiet</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <developmentalStageFilter>Adult</developmentalStageFilter>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>it has been quiet</label>
        <description>Nothing for weeks. That is good. That is what we wanted. I cannot make myself enjoy it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-2</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>too quiet for too long</label>
        <description>It has been so long now that the quiet is the thing making me nervous. Something is owed. Somebody is going to come and collect it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-5</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    The other direction, and the reason this mod is not only a punishment.

    A colonist who is armed, armoured and standing behind something feels better than a colonist
    with nothing, in the same colony, on the same day. It is the one lever in the set that a
    player pulls by doing the thing the game already wanted them to do.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>DR_Steady</defName>
    <workerClass>Dread.ThoughtWorker_Steady</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <developmentalStageFilter>Adult</developmentalStageFilter>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>we can hold this</label>
        <description>Walls up, guns loaded, everybody fed and standing. Let them come and find out.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    Somebody who cannot wait. Bloodlust is normally a way of not minding the worst thing that
    happened; here it is a way of looking forward to the worst thing that has not.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>DR_Sharpening</defName>
    <workerClass>Dread.ThoughtWorker_Sharpening</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <developmentalStageFilter>Adult</developmentalStageFilter>
    <requiredTraits>
      <li>Bloodlust</li>
    </requiredTraits>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>something is coming</label>
        <description>Everybody else has gone quiet and started checking the doors. I have cleaned my gun twice. I hope they are big ones.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>6</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    Pointed at one person: the ones you are glad are here.

    The first purely positive social thought in the set. Everything else that changes an opinion
    in these mods takes it down. This one goes up, and it goes up for the colonist who can
    actually fight - which is a thing the base game has never once noticed anybody doing.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>DR_StandsBetween</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Dread.Thought_Relieved</thoughtClass>
    <workerClass>Dread.ThoughtWorker_StandsBetween</workerClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <developmentalStageFilter>Adult</developmentalStageFilter>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>glad they are here</label>
        <baseOpinionOffset>12</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>they are what stands between us and it</label>
        <baseOpinionOffset>22</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
